\par\par \uc2 Real Estate Desk; SECTRE\par \b \uc2 Overheated Rental Market in Florida\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gregory Schmidt \par \uc2 372 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 July 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Demand for apartments in Florida has intensified, followed by markets in Pennsylvania and New Jersey, as Americans embrace remote work.\par \par \uc2 As pandemic restrictions ease and remote work becomes a permanent fixture, Americans continue to seek homes in communities with more relaxed lifestyles -- particularly in Florida and the Northeast, home to the country's most competitive markets for renters, according to a new analysis of real estate data.\par \par \uc2 The analysis, released in June by RentCafe, a division of the real estate software firm \uc2 Yardi Systems\uc2 , showed that Miami-Dade County, home to more than 20 miles of beaches, was the most competitive area for renters during the first four months of 2022. Also among the Top 10: Harrisburg, Pa.; Orlando, Fla.; North and Central Jersey, Southwest Florida, Grand Rapids, Mich.; Rochester, N.Y., and Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 The rental trend has been fueled in part by stubbornly high house prices and rising mortgage rates, which are pushing would-be buyers into an already overheated rental market, the report said. To determine the hottest markets so far this year, researchers considered five metrics: average vacant days, occupancy levels, prospective renters competing for listings, lease renewal rates, and the volume of new apartments built in the first four months of the year.\par \par \uc2 Various factors influenced the outcome, including rapid inflation and the rise of remote work, said Doug Ressler, manager of business intelligence for Yardi Matrix, a division of \uc2 Yardi Systems\uc2 . ''It would be nice in these mosaics if one thing contributed to growing demand,'' he said, ''but each market has its own profile.''\par \par \uc2 For instance, Miami-Dade County expanded its housing inventory from January to April to accommodate an influx of renters. But the lure of looser Covid restrictions and low taxes kept the area highly competitive. ''Miami has a business-friendly climate,'' Mr. Ressler said.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Harrisburg -- which is close to Philadelphia, New York and Washington -- added no new apartments in the same period, prompting tenants to stay put and renew their leases.\par \par \uc2 Miami-Dade County was the top draw for renters during the first four months of 2022, according to a new report. (PHOTOGRAPH BY LYNNE SLADKY/ASSOCIATED PRESS) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220710ei7a0003j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
