\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Buttigieg, With Covid, Will Work From Home\b0\par\par\uc2 By Johnny Diaz \par \uc2 460 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 June 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 18\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mr. Buttigieg, who a White House spokesman said was not considered a close contact of President Biden, is at least the fifth cabinet secretary to test positive in about the last month.\par \par \uc2 Transportation Secretary Pete Buttigieg said on Monday that he had tested positive for the coronavirus, the latest member of President Biden's cabinet to be infected.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Buttigieg added that he was experiencing mild symptoms.\par \par \uc2 ''I plan to work remotely while isolating according to \uc2 C.D.C\uc2 . guidelines, and look forward to when I can safely return to the office and the road,'' he wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , referring to guidance from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Buttigieg was not considered a close contact of Mr. Biden, a White House spokesman said on Monday. To be a close contact, Mr. Buttigieg would have to have been less than six feet away from Mr. Biden for 15 minutes or more in a 24-hour period, according to the \uc2 C.D.C\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Department of Transportation said on Monday that Mr. Buttigieg, 40, has been vaccinated and boosted.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Buttigieg is one of at least 15 people who have tested positive for the coronavirus after attending the Mackinac Policy Conference in Michigan last week, according to the Detroit Regional Chamber, which organized the event. It is difficult to determine exactly how or when someone was exposed to and infected with the virus.\par \par \uc2 ''The individuals testing positive report being asymptomatic or experiencing mild symptoms, and we wish them a speedy recovery,'' the Detroit Regional Chamber said in a statement on Monday. In all, there were 1,347 attendees and support staff at the event, which ran from May 31 to June 3. They had to submit proof of vaccination or a negative P.C.R. test to attend the conference.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  of Michigan, who also attended the event and spent time with Mr. Buttigieg, took a rapid test on Monday morning, ''which came back negative,'' according to Bobby Leddy, a spokesman. Mr. Leddy said that Ms. Whitmer, 50, ''is fully up-to-date on her vaccinations, and is not currently experiencing any symptoms.''\par \par \uc2 Last week, Labor Secretary \uc2 Martin J. Walsh\uc2  and Interior Secretary \uc2 Deb Haaland\uc2  announced that they had also received positive test results.\par \par \uc2 Others in Mr. Biden's inner circle who have tested positive in about the past month include Secretary of State \uc2 Antony J. Blinken\uc2 , Health and Human Services Secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , and Susan Rice, the White House domestic policy adviser. Mr. Biden's daughter, Ashley Biden, was also infected, in mid-May.\par \par \uc2 Pete Buttigieg is the latest cabinet member to be infected. (PHOTOGRAPH BY LEIGH VOGEL FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220607ei670004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
