\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Union at \uc2 Vox\uc2  Vows to Strike If Talks Fail\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Robertson \par \uc2 450 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 June 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Vox Media Union's contract expires at midnight on June 13. The union is seeking cost-of-living raises and affordable benefits.\par \par \uc2 The union that covers about 350 workers at \uc2 Vox Media\uc2 , the publisher of websites including Recode, Eater and SB Nation, said on Wednesday that its members had signed a strike pledge as negotiations over a contract went down to the wire.\par \par \uc2 The Vox Media Union's contract expires at midnight on June 13. Union members said the company had not yet agreed to its proposals. A strike pledge means the members are ready to strike if the union calls for one if a deal can't be reached.\par \par \uc2 Seth Rosenthal, a video producer for Secret Base, SB Nation's \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channel, said the union was seeking competitive salary minimums, cost-of-living raises and affordable benefits, as well as measures to acknowledge workers' longevity at the company and a commitment to protect those proposals in case of a corporate sale or merger.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Rosenthal said that in April 2020, early in the coronavirus pandemic, \uc2 Vox Media\uc2  had asked staff to give up their contractual salary increases for the year but never compensated them for that later.\par \par \uc2 ''Since then, \uc2 Vox Media\uc2  has expanded its business and made multiple large acquisitions, but our unit members have not been made whole for their sacrifice,'' said Mr. Rosenthal, a member of the union's bargaining committee.\par \par \uc2 Lauren Starke, a \uc2 Vox Media\uc2  spokeswoman, said in an email: ''We are actively engaged in bargaining, and, with bargaining scheduled on most days through the expiration of the contract, hope to reach a resolution at the table that we are all proud of.''\par \par \uc2 Ms. Starke said there was no annual pay increase in 2020 across the entire company.\par \par \uc2 The negotiations are taking place as consumer prices are rising at their fastest pace in four decades and housing costs across the country are climbing faster than wages.\par \par \uc2 ''People are getting priced out of their homes and experiencing financial hardship because their salaries are totally failing to keep up with inflation,'' said Caitlin PenzeyMoog, a senior copy editor at Vox.com and a member of the bargaining committee.\par \par \uc2 The union, which formed in 2018, covers editorial and video staff across \uc2 Vox Media\uc2  sites, including Vox.com, SB Nation, Curbed, Eater, Polygon, Recode and The Verge.\par \par \uc2 It doesn't include staff at New York magazine, which the company also owns. That publication's union agreed to its first contract with the company in January, after two and a half years of negotiations.\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY Richard Vogel/Associated Press FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220602ei620004e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
